   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The Perfekt with haben",
     "texto": [
      "Most German verbs form the compound past (**Perfekt**) with the auxiliary verb **haben** in the present plus the **past participle** (Partizip II), which must go **at the end** of the sentence.",
      "With regular verbs, the participle is formed by adding the prefix **ge-** to the stem and ending in **-t** (or **-et** after -d/-t): lernen → **gelernt**, kochen → **gekocht**, hören → **gehört**, spielen → **gespielt**.",
      "Irregular or strong verbs usually end in **-en** and sometimes change their vowel: schreiben → **geschrieben**, essen → **gegessen**, lesen → **gelesen**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
